      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Mark Ruffalo, as the meme humorously implies that the actor (who plays the Hulk) is 'in the sheets' (private, intimate) while the character he portrays (the Hulk) is 'in the streets' (public, active). The user identifies with the actor's private life as contrasted with the public persona of the character. This projection is implicit, not explicit, and relies on the user's understanding of the actor's role and the pun.",
